#! nimbus: desktop-recommends
# =============================================================================
# 25-desktop-extras.list.chroot - applications and conveniences (recommended)
# =============================================================================
# What: the standard KDE applications, Discover with its built-in PackageKit
#       backend and Flatpak, the two browsers, Bluetooth, and everyday
#       command-line tools.
# Why:  spec section 1 (Apps row). They are in the image, but users may
#       reasonably remove any of them, and doing so must not remove
#       nimbusos-desktop. So the metapackage Recommends these (marker line
#       above; docs/PLAN.md NOTE-48). apt never reinstalls a recommended
#       package the user removed, but it does install packages that a later
#       NimbusOS release newly recommends. Chromium is also a hard dependency
#       of nimbus-control, because it runs the Control Center window.
# Format rules: see 10-base.list.chroot.
# =============================================================================

# KDE's full application set and settings extras
kde-plasma-desktop
kde-config-sddm
bluedevil
kinfocenter
breeze-gtk-theme

# Applications
konsole
dolphin
kate
ark
okular
gwenview
kde-spectacle

# Software centre: Discover with PackageKit (built in) and Flatpak backends
plasma-discover
plasma-discover-backend-flatpak
packagekit
flatpak

# Browsers
firefox-esr
chromium

# Bluetooth
bluez
libspa-0.2-bluetooth

# Command-line conveniences
bash-completion
man-db
less
nano
curl
gpg
openssh-client
